1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:11,497
This ovule is turned completely upside down on its stalk, so the micropyle lies right beside the hilum, and the funicle is fused along one side as a ridge, the raphe.

2
00:00:11,497 --> 00:00:17,916
That is an anatropous ovule, the commonest type, found in about eighty percent of families.

